ranges.text:
{
  "game": "New Angeles",
  "scope": "FFG2016 base4–6; complete setup; official2018FAQ",
  "benchmark_version": "seed-v2",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "Q01",
      "question": "Describe complete core setup: which decks are separated, how the starting city and turn track are determined, the initial round/resource/threat/capital positions, corporation sides and cards, rival allocation, and the initial investment choice. Exclude the simplified first-game setup."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q02",
      "question": "What action cards does each corporation draw in four-player and five/six-player games, in what order, and how are General draws selected? Include Melange."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q03",
      "question": "Describe the active player’s turn, including start-of-turn asset timing, Refresh, end-of-turn abilities, hand limit and passing. When does the Action Phase end and must every player have a turn that round?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q04",
      "question": "List the five deal steps and the order of effect, asset claim and cleanup. Which asset is revealed and can the active player pass on the main offer?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q05",
      "question": "The first, second and third counteroffers are proposed in one deal. How many hand cards must each proposer discard in addition to their offer? Can the active player counter, can an earlier proposer later support, and is there another circuit of counteroffers?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q06",
      "question": "In a deal with a counteroffer, who may support, how are cards committed and counted, may a player support both or add more later, and who wins a2–2 tie? What happens if nobody counteroffers?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q07",
      "question": "How can an emergency be proposed or used as support, does it count toward hand size or hand-card theft, and where/state does a stolen emergency return after winning or losing an offer? What may Bryan Stinson steal?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q08",
      "question": "An exploited district prints primary2 credits and secondary1 entertainment, has a development, an orgcrime unit and is in protest. What does it produce and what is its resulting unrest? How would starting in strike or outage change production, and do non-android districts produce in the normal Production Phase?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q09",
      "question": "When an android district with Human First is exploited, what happens from stable, protest, strike, and already-outage starting states? Is an ordinary failed unrest increase without Human First enough to cause an outage?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q10",
      "question": "An orgcrime unit is placed into a district already containing orgcrime and its route then meets a prisec-protected district before eventually reaching the Root. Explain its movement, reserve/threat result and contract consequences. How do android moves differ?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q11",
      "question": "When does illness add threat during an action, including chosen districts and failed placements/moves? If several ill districts are involved is the increase multiplied? Do production or events trigger illness, and what does an illness token entering the Root do?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q12",
      "question": "State each corporation’s contract payment and trigger, who may resolve the triggering action, and the important Haas-Bioroid, NBN, Root and Melange exceptions."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q13",
      "question": "What may players trade or give away, what items cannot be traded after the official erratum, and when are immediate, future-promise, disputed-binding and three-player trades binding? Does an exhausted traded asset ready?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q14",
      "question": "Explain asset timing when several abilities share a timing, what is optional, when exhausted assets ready, and whether a newly gained End of Turn asset can be used this turn. How often can each End of Turn ability be used?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q15",
      "question": "Give the full demand-round order, including what happens when only one resource misses its target, when supplies reset and unchosen investments go, and which steps are omitted in the third demand round."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q16",
      "question": "The third demand fails and pushes threat to25. Does investment scoring happen first, and who wins if the Federalist has25 capital? Contrast finishing that demand below25, a tie with your named rival, and having your own rival card at4 versus5–6 players."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q17",
      "question": "Which information may players communicate about action hands, hand counts, rival cards, investments, hidden turn-track assets, and event cards seen through a reorder effect? What does Thomas Haas require you to announce?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q18",
      "question": "Where do discarded action cards, assets and removed components go? What happens if an action deck is empty when a card must be drawn, a reserve component runs out, or production would pass the track end?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q19",
      "question": "How are a standard round’s phases ordered, which districts get exploited and in what order, and how is an event resolved, discarded and used to set the next turn track? Must that track be reset after the sixth standard round?"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q20",
      "question": "Is resolving Liquidation exploitation, and which production modifiers apply? How do Unorthodox Knowledge and Caprice Nisei interact, including whether the resolving player is bound by the announced resolution?"
    }
  ]
}
